### 3. MISSING ORG SCOPE IN TEMPLATE SERVICE READS (HIGH)

**Location:** `/src/services/TemplateService.js` (line 143-146, 155-158)

**Issue:** `getByOrg()` and `getById()` do not enforce organization scope for non-admin users.

**Code Analysis:**
```javascript
async getByOrg(organizationId) {
  this._requireAuth();
  // ← Missing: _assertOrgScope(actor, organizationId)
  return this._repo.findByOrg(organizationId);
}

async getById(templateId) {
  this._requireAuth();
  // ← Missing scope check
  return this._repo.findById(templateId);
}
```

**Attack Vector:**
1. STORE_MANAGER in store-001 calls `templateService.getByOrg('store-002')`
2. Returns all templates from store-002 (notification content, variable placeholders, business messaging)
3. No audit trail of cross-org access

**Remediation Priority:** HIGH  
**Recommended Fix:**
```javascript
async getByOrg(organizationId) {
  const actor = this._requireAuth();
  this._assertOrgScope(actor, organizationId);
  return this._repo.findByOrg(organizationId);
}

async getById(templateId) {
  const actor = this._requireAuth();
  const template = await this._repo.findById(templateId);
  if (template && actor.role !== ROLES.ADMINISTRATOR) {
    this._assertOrgScope(actor, template.organizationId);
  }
  return template;
}
```

