### 9. BOOTSTRAP DOESN'T VALIDATE UNIQUENESS OF INITIAL ADMIN USERNAME (LOW)

**Location:** `/src/services/BootstrapService.js` (line 54-117)

**Issue:** Bootstrap creates the first admin without checking if a user already exists with that username.

**Code Analysis:**
```javascript
async bootstrap({ adminUsername, adminPassword, orgName }) {
  if (await this.isBootstrapped()) {
    throw new Error('System is already initialized...');
  }
  // ...
  // Creates user without checking username uniqueness
  await this._userRepo.create(adminUser);
}
```

**Risk:** If bootstrap is called twice in rapid succession (race condition) before the first write completes, two admin users could be created with the same username.

**Remediation Priority:** LOW (single-tab app, race conditions unlikely; database add() will fail on duplicate unique index)

