## SOLID SECURITY CONTROLS (STRENGTHS)

### 1. Comprehensive RBAC with Bypass Pattern
- All services implement `_requireRole()` with ADMINISTRATOR bypass
- Guest role properly restricted from writes (test at `/tests/unit/permissionGuards.test.js:216-233`)
- Tested across 5 roles: ADMINISTRATOR, STORE_MANAGER, ANALYST, REVIEWER, GUEST

### 2. Login Lockout (15 minutes, 5 failed attempts)
- Implements `failedLoginAttempts` tracking
- Prevents username enumeration (generic error message: "Invalid username or password")
- Re-lock timer persists across tab reloads via broadcast channel

### 3. Session Unlock Brute-Force Protection
- Max 5 unlock attempts before forced logout
- Counter resets on successful unlock or full login
- Well-tested (`/tests/unit/unlockHardening.test.js`)

### 4. Encryption Architecture
- AES-256-GCM with 96-bit random IV
- PBKDF2 with 310,000 iterations for password hashing
- Session key cleared on lock (separate from password salt)
- Key rotation on password change re-encrypts all sensitive fields

### 5. Audit Trail (Append-only)
- All domain actions logged to immutable store
- Protected from import/export (in `PROTECTED_STORES` set)
- No update/delete capability (only create)

### 6. Validation Depth
- Input validation functions check type, length, format, enum membership
- Placeholder validation prevents injection in templates
- Outcome code validation for risk case resolution
- Post-substitution template length check for compact notices

### 7. State Machine Enforcement
- Order transitions validated against `ORDER_TRANSITIONS` map
- Ticket status transitions strictly enforced
- Terminal states (COMPLETED, CLOSED) prevent further transitions
- Risk cases cannot transition from RESOLVED/DISMISSED back to OPEN

### 8. Organization Scope Enforcement (Mostly)
- `_assertOrgScope()` prevents STORE_MANAGER from accessing cross-org data in 11/13 services
- Admin always bypasses scope checks
- Subtree traversal for hierarchical access control

